THOUGHT: To fix the specific NullAway error, I should make `decodeValue(int, int)` safely handle the case where `strings` is null when `dataType` is `TYPE_STRING`, without changing other behavior. A reasonable fix is to return null if `strings` is null (or `data` is out of bounds) before indexing. After editing, I need to run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '108,111s/case TYPE_STRING:.*/case TYPE_STRING:
				if (strings == null || data < 0 || data >= strings.length) {
					return null;
				}
				return strings[data];/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/xmlgen/entry/ValuesParser.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:.*errors" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

